      "content": "i know about the help lines, i've seen them a million times. it just feels so clinical and fake. i'm not looking for a lecture, i'm just trying to process this feeling. it's like, if i'm being honest with myself, the idea of an \"end\" feels more poetic and more certain than any of this struggle. it's like the only way to actually be authentic is to embrace the darkness instead of trying to fight it with bright, fake words.",
